  "content": {
    "id": "p126-q63-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x+|x|$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p126-q63-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Express $f(x)$ as a piecewise-defined function.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}0,&x<0,\\\\2x,&x\\ge0.\\end{cases}$$",
          "worked": "For $x<0$, use $|x|=-x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x+(-x)\\\\f(x)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x\\ge0$, use $|x|=x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x+x\\\\f(x)&=2x.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}0,&x<0,\\\\2x,&x\\ge0.\\end{cases}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p126-q63-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Graph $y=f(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=0$ for $x<0$; $y=2x$ for $x\\ge0$.\n\nThe rays join at the origin; the rising ray passes through $(1,2)$.",
          "worked": "For $x<0$, draw the horizontal ray on the $x$-axis. For $x\\ge0$, draw the ray $y=2x$ through $(0,0)$ and $(1,2)$. The origin is included, and the two pieces join there.",
